PLACEHOLDER — NOT a real OCI image tar (ADR-0054).

This <1 KB committed stand-in exists only so go:embed has a file at compile time and
embedimg.Tar("nodejs22") returns a non-empty reader (the ADR-0054 non-gated unit test).

The REAL per-arch distroless OCI image tar is built at release/integration time by
'just build-runtime-images' (docker build -> docker save, gzip -9) and overwrites this
file before the binary ships. Importing it into the managed containerd (client.Import)
is the Linux+root integration lane — never exercised by 'just ci'.

See internal/runtime/embedimg/README.md for the placeholder/release pattern.
